<title>USA: Two ex-officials of Sequa unit sentenced for fraud.</title>
<headline>Two ex-officials of Sequa unit sentenced for fraud.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two former executive vice presidents of Chromalloy Gas Turbine Corp.'s research and technology division were sentenced Tuesday on fraud charges related to the repair of aircraft engine parts.</p>
<p>Chromalloy is a unit of Sequa Corp..</p>
<p>James Gabriel was sentenced to three years in prison and fined $500,000, and Gerard Vitti was sentenced to six months of home confinement and fined $30,000.</p>
<p>The men were sentenced by U.S. District Judge Jed Rakoff in White Plains, N.Y.</p>
